    steps: ["An invoice is Overdue when it isn't a draft, isn't Paid, still has a balance, and its Due date has passed (the day after, by your device's date).", "Payment plans are checked per installment: overdue only when an unpaid installment's date has passed. Later installments not yet due don't count.", "Partly paid invoices count by the remaining balance. Deposits already paid lower it.", "The dashboard Overdue card shows the count (for example '3 overdue') or 'No overdue invoices'. Documents → Overdue and Collect use the same rule.", "Setting the status to Overdue yourself doesn't make it overdue before a due date that hasn't passed."],
